From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:58:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usage: a reported call can carry first_text_ms and flow_ms
 (#2637)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A reporter that calls its vendor itself times its own calls, but
POST /v1/magpie/usage/requests refused a record carrying
first_text_ms ("not a field a reported record takes"), the field
usage.jsonl has for the reply's first text. DecodeOf times a
reasoning reply's answer from its first text, so without it almost
every reported reasoning call shows "—" for its answer speed on the
Requests page; flow_ms, which lets the held-and-released-in-a-burst
guard (HeldShare) run on a reported row, was refused the same way.
Both are now taken, checked like ttft_ms (a whole number of ms, at
most a day) and written as they came, so the page's speed, HeldShare
and ThinkPace see what a gateway call sees. Existing reporters that
send neither are unaffected.

What changed:
- internal/gateway/usage_ingest.go: ingestFields takes first_text_ms
  and flow_ms; parseReported reads each into the record through the
  same whole() check ttft_ms goes through.
- docs/subsystems/gateway-sessions.md: the ingest field list names
  them.

Run (at origin/main 8bb9375e7, go1.26.x darwin/arm64):
- New TestUsageIngestFirstTextAndFlow: red before ("record 0:
  first_text_ms: not a field a reported record takes (...)"), the
  issue's repro; green after, and the reported row reads back with
  first_text_ms 4700 and flow_ms 300, negative, fractional,
  quoted and over-a-day values refused by field name.
- Ablation: with internal/gateway/usage_ingest.go alone put back to
  8bb9375e7 (test kept), the new test goes red with the same 400;
  restored, green again (-count=1).
- GOTOOLCHAIN=auto go test -tags nogui -p 2 -run TestUsageIngest
  ./internal/gateway: ok. -run 'Decode|Speed|TTFT' ./internal/usage:
  ok. gofmt -l clean. go vet ./... (darwin), GOOS=linux and
  GOOS=windows go vet -tags nogui ./...: clean (internal/gui's
  trayimage cgo Wenum-conversion warning as on main). Builds for
  darwin, linux (nogui) and windows (nogui): ok (darwin ld's
  duplicate-library warnings as on main).

Not tried: a real reporter's dashboard view (the record shape is
checked at the ingest boundary and read back through the GET route).

Fixes #2637

